{"session_id": "wsess_63072782e639", "ts_start": "2026-06-15T07:30:51Z", "ts_end": "2026-06-15T07:32:51Z", "model": "qwen3.5:9b", "task": "Use wren_retrieve query='production grade godot cockpit feature 11' k=4 then write a multi-paragraph proposal (150+ words) for one specific improvement. Stamp F47 'wren_push_11' with your proposal text.", "turns": 3, "tool_calls": [{"turn": 1, "fn": "wren_retrieve", "args": {"query": "production grade godot cockpit feature 11", "k": 4}, "result_len": 5123}, {"turn": 2, "fn": "wren_stamp_f47_record", "args": {"kind": "wren_push_11", "summary": "PROPOSAL: Implement Worker View Mode Toggle in Godot Cockpit\n\nThe Godot cockpit currently displays worker density badges but lacks a view-mode toggle for granular inspection. This proposal introduces a Worker View Mode switch in the bottom command bar that cycles through three visualization presets: (1) Density Badges \u2014 current default showing worker count per floor with color-coded saturation; (2) Worker Cards \u2014 expands each badge into a compact card showing worker name, role, and status indicator; (3) Inspector Overlay \u2014 activates the selected floor inspector panel with full telemetry readout for the highlighted worker.\n\nImplementation requires adding a new EnumNode for view_mode (0=badges, 1=cards, 2=inspector) in the HUD autoload, wiring a ToggleButton in the bottom bar to cycle modes, and updating the WorkerPanelNode to respect the current mode. The cards view needs a GridContainer with scrollable overflow, while inspector mode requires the existing InspectorPanelNode to dock over the central 3D scene.\n\nThis enhancement transforms the cockpit from a status dashboard into an operational command center where Ross can quickly scan floor occupancy, drill into specific workers, or toggle to full inspector mode for deep diagnostics. The toggle should persist across sessions via the registry. Estimated effort: 2-3 hours. This closes the gap between prototype and production-grade cockpit, enabling Ross to manage the 53-floor tower with surgical precision rather than just broad overview."}, "result_len": 29}], "wall_seconds": 119.46, "final_text": "Proposal stamped to F47 as `wren_push_11`. The Worker View Mode toggle would transform the cockpit from a status dashboard into an operational command center, enabling Ross to cycle between density badges, worker cards, and inspector overlay modes for surgical floor management."}
