{"session_id": "wsess_a20242f181ad", "ts_start": "2026-06-23T08:59:18Z", "ts_end": "2026-06-23T08:59:33Z", "model": "qwen3.5:9b", "task": "Wren \u2014 narrow ask. The Binance over-trade is real (ETH 9655 closes / 26 real = 9629 rate-limit rejections). The broker gate (data/registries/qsb_broker_placement_gate.json) caps Binance at 120/hr. We have 3 binance workers + 1 strategy demo = 4. 120 / 4 = 30 opens/hr per worker maximum. Give me ONE specific thing: what's the simplest pre-open check to add to qsb_belief_driven_trader.py so a worker tracks its own open-rate and STOPS opening when it has placed 30 opens in the trailing 60 minutes? Return: (a) the per-worker class attribute to add (name + type), (b) the helper method body (~6 lines max), (c) where in _open_position to add the guard. Keep it tight.", "turns": 1, "tool_calls": [], "wall_seconds": 14.78, "final_text": "This is a straightforward rate-limit guard. Here's the minimal implementation:\n\n**(a) Per-worker class attribute:**\n```python\nself._open_window_count: int = 0\nself._open_window_start: datetime = datetime.now()\n```\n\n**(b) Helper method body (~6 lines):**\n```python\ndef _check_rate_limit(self) -> bool:\n    now = datetime.now()\n    if now - self._open_window_start > timedelta(minutes=60):\n        self._open_window_count = 0\n        self._open_window_start = now\n    if self._open_window_count >= 30:\n        return False\n    self._open_window_count += 1\n    return True\n```\n\n**(c) Where in `_open_position` to add the guard:**\nAt the very start of `_open_position()`, before any Binance API call:\n\n```python\ndef _open_position(self, symbol: str, side: str, qty: float, ...) -> Position:\n    if not self._check_rate_limit():\n        raise RateLimitExceeded(\"Binance: 30 opens in trailing 60 min\")\n    # ... rest of open logic\n```\n\n**Placement:** Insert immediately after method signature, before `self._log(\"opening\", ...)` or any `self._place_order()` call."}
