ty state without reading numbers. High-energy traders stand out visually during active trading periods.\n\n---\n\n### **UPGRADE 2: Mood-Based Avatar Emojis**\n**(a) Concrete Effect:** Dynamic emoji overlay next to each trader avatar changes based on `mood` word (e.g., \"confident\" \u2192 \ud83d\ude0e, \"cautious\" \u2192 \ud83e\udd14, \"frustrated\" \u2192 \ud83d\ude24, \"calm\" \u2192 \ud83d\ude0c).\n\n**(b) DOM Element:** `.trader-avatar .mood-emoji` span within each trader card.\n\n**(c) Data Source:** `character.json` \u2192 `mood` field.\n\n**(d) Why Better:** Adds personality and emotional context. Ross can spot team morale issues at a glance. Makes 44 traders feel like a team, not just numbers.\n\n---\n\n### **UPGRADE 3: Win-Rate Bar with Color Gradient**\n**(a) Concrete Effect:** Horizontal bar under each trader chart. Color gradient: green (high win-rate) \u2192 yellow \u2192 red (low). Bar fills smoothly on update.\n\n**(b) DOM Element:** `.trader-card .win-rate-bar` div.\n\n**(c) Data Source:** Dashboard chart data \u2192 win-rate percentage.\n\n**(d) Why Better:** Replaces static text with visual progress. Color coding lets Ross scan performance in <2s. Smooth animation on data refresh prevents jarring updates.\n\n---\n\n### **UPGRADE 4: BUY/SELL Feed with Trader Attribution**\n**(a) Concrete Effect:** Each BUY/SELL event scrolls with a small trader avatar icon + name. Events from active traders (energy > 5) get a subtle highlight glow.\n\n**(b) DOM Element:** `.feed-container .event-item` within the live journal.\n\n**(c) Data Source:** Live bus events + `character.json` for trader identity.\n\n**(d) Why Better:** Connects market action to individual traders. Ross sees who's driving the market. Attribution makes the feed less abstract and more actionable.\n\n---\n\n**WREN VISUAL TOP 4**"}
