{"session_id": "wsess_fc69750a379e", "ts_start": "2026-06-23T11:34:23Z", "ts_end": "2026-06-23T11:34:56Z", "model": "qwen3.5:9b", "task": "Wren \u2014 Binance traders BTC/ETH/BNB still losing (~30% wr after our throttle fix this morning). Throttle stopped phantom cycling but underlying loss-per-trade remains. Top losses today are -\u00a365 stop_loss_2sigma. The exit math (2\u03c3 stop + min-hold) may be too tight for crypto's spikes vs FX. Pick ONE structural improvement we should try for Binance specifically (not FX). End: 'WREN BINANCE FIX:'.", "turns": 2, "tool_calls": [{"turn": 1, "fn": "wren_dispatch_f46_team", "args": {"member": "all", "task": "design structural improvement for Binance BTC/ETH/BNB traders to reduce loss-per-trade after throttle fix, focusing on crypto volatility/spikes vs FX"}, "result_len": 1877}], "wall_seconds": 33.34, "final_text": "WREN BINANCE FIX: Implement **volatility-adjusted dynamic stops** for Binance BTC/ETH/BNB. Replace static 2\u03c3 with **2\u03c3 \u00d7 (crypto_volatility_index / FX_volatility_index)**, where crypto_volatility_index is derived from 15m BTC/ETH realized volatility. This scales stops 2-4\u00d7 wider during crypto spikes vs FX, preventing premature exits on normal volatility. Pair with **spike-aware min-hold**: extend hold time by 30-60% when volatility index exceeds 1.5\u00d7 baseline. This preserves the throttle fix while accounting for crypto's inherent volatility regime difference from FX."}
