{"session_id": "wsess_11987f15e80f", "ts_start": "2026-06-25T11:15:39Z", "ts_end": "2026-06-25T11:15:47Z", "model": "qwen2.5:7b-instruct", "task": "URGENT TWO-BUG diagnosis. Ross wants ALL workers firing (he sees 35/93). Root cause: belief_updater is starved because trade.closed events arent flowing. Two bugs:\n\nBUG 1: BUS SUBSCRIBER DISCONNECT CHURN\n- tools/qsb_event_bus.py write_event() does asyncio.wait_for(w.drain(), timeout=0.5)\n- If drain takes >0.5s the writer is killed\n- Subscribers reconnect every 30s \u2014 visible in bus.log: \"subscriber disconnected (uds)\" + \"subscriber connected (uds)\" every ~30s\n- Sample bus.log: 11:02:41 disconnect, 11:02:51 connect, 11:02:54 connect, 11:02:57 disconnect... constant churn\n- Tick rate is ~50/sec across 3 venues = 150 events/sec. drain() may legitimately take >0.5s under load.\n- When disconnected, worker publish() raises but the worker doesn't reconnect cleanly to the BUS (subscriber.publish writes to self.writer which may be a closed socket \u2192 silently lost? or raises and is caught somewhere?)\n\nBUG 2: BINANCE QTY PRECISION\n- Sample failure: qty=0.0003690369874921267 (16 decimals) \u2192 HTTP 400 from Binance\n- Binance step size is 0.00001 (5 decimals)\n- Code in qsb_broker_place.py uses math.floor for qty but apparently doesnt clamp to step size\n\nTHREE QUESTIONS \u2014 answer + SIGNOFF:\n\nQ1 \u2014 bus disconnect fix: pick best option\n(a) Raise drain timeout to 2.0s (relax the hangup)\n(b) Make broadcast non-blocking (fire-and-forget) \u2014 drop the await drain\n(c) Per-subscriber bounded write queue with separate consumer task\n(d) Heartbeat keepalive every 10s to keep connections warm\n\nQ2 \u2014 Binance qty fix:\n(a) Round qty DOWN to nearest 0.00001 in broker_place before placing\n(b) Lookup symbol stepSize via /api/v3/exchangeInfo and use exact rounding\n(c) Hardcode per-symbol step in a dict\n\nQ3 \u2014 Are workers reconnecting cleanly?\n- qsb_event_subscriber.py run() handles connection