ll_seconds": 7.19, "final_text": "RECAP:\nSkyscraperHQ is a digital tower with 169 floors, each representing a department or model. The project's public face is the github.com/devon3dp/skyscraperhq repository, which currently supports web and shop functionalities. Inside the tower, models like Claude, Wren, and OpenAI operate on specific floors to manage various tasks.\n\nTraders work across F41 (OANDA practice), F42 (Binance testnet), and F43 (Alpaca paper) for practice trading. These floors are part of a larger event-driven architecture that feeds market data into belief state updates, regime detection, and ensemble coordination to drive trading decisions.\n\nCURRENT WEB DASHBOARD:\nThe existing web dashboard at localhost:8847 already displays gauges, Sankey flow diagrams, streaming waveforms, and other panels for real-time trader performance. It is production-ready but lacks the immersive 3D environment Ross envisions.\n\nUE5 AMBITION:\n\"Trading data inside the floors with 3D working interior\" means integrating market data into a 3D building where each floor represents an instrument's trading environment. Traders would work in these interiors, and all relevant data (charts, info boards, chat logs) would be visible within their respective floors.\n\nRISKS:\nLifting and shifting the current web dashboard into UE5 involves significant costs: engine extraction, data wiring for real-time updates, scene building, asset import, and ongoing operational support. The risk of losing existing functionality during this transition is high.\n\nPROPOSAL:\nRecommend a smarter staging approach where we first prototype key features in UE5 with minimal changes to the current system. This allows us to validate the concept without fully committing resources.\n\nAGREEMENT:\nI DISAGREE and want to proceed with a staged approach, starting with a UE5 prototype before full extraction.\n\nSIGNOFF: Wren reports \u2014 Recommend staged approach for UE5 integration."}
