{"session_id": "wsess_f1efe153076f", "ts_start": "2026-06-28T13:56:33Z", "ts_end": "2026-06-28T13:57:47Z", "model": "qwen3.5:9b", "task": "QSB UE5 city block has central tower + neighbors + 40 trees + 12 cars + 8 bus stops + 40 hydrants/benches. UnrealMCP plugin on TCP 127.0.0.1:55557 accepts JSON commands. The 'create_actor' command supports mesh param (Cube/Cylinder/Sphere/Cone/Plane) and also full path /Engine/EditorMeshes/Camera/SM_CineCam etc. YOUR JOB: use wren_bash to write a Python script /tmp/wren_build_park.py that adds a PARK to the city: 1) a 30m \u00d7 30m grass plane at (4000,-4000,1), 2) 8 sphere bushes around its perimeter (mesh=Sphere), 3) a fountain at park center (cylinder base + sphere top), 4) 6 picnic tables (cube tops + 4 cone legs each). Name everything V8_Park_*. Then run the script. Use wren_bash. Take action \u2014 don't just propose.", "turns": 4, "tool_calls": [{"turn": 1, "fn": "wren_bash", "args": {"cmd": "cat > /tmp/wren_build_park.py << 'EOF'\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport json\nimport socket\nimport time\n\nHOST = \"127.0.0.1\"\nPORT = 55557\n\ndef send_command(cmd):\n    \"\"\"Send a command to UnrealMCP and return response\"\"\"\n    sock = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_STREAM)\n    sock.connect((HOST, PORT))\n    sock.sendall(json.dumps(cmd).encode() + b\"\\n\")\n    response = b\"\"\n    while True:\n        chunk = sock.recv(4096)\n        if not chunk:\n            break\n        response += chunk\n        if b\"\\n\" in response:\n            response = response.split(b\"\\n\")[-1] + b\"\\n\"\n            break\n    sock.close()\n    return json.loads(response.decode())\n\ndef create_actor(mesh, x, y, z, name, **kwargs):\n    \"\"\"Create an actor with given mesh at position\"\"\"\n    cmd = {\n        \"command\": \"create_actor\",\n        \"mesh\": mesh,\n        \"position\": [x, y, z],\n        \"name\": name,\n        **kwargs\n    }\n    return send_command(cmd)\n\n# 1) 30m \u00d7 30m grass plane at (4000,