{"session_id": "wsess_399d3e7096ca", "ts_start": "2026-07-02T20:40:13Z", "ts_end": "2026-07-02T20:40:49Z", "model": "qwen3.5:9b", "task": "STRICT: your first action MUST be to call the wren_read_file tool on path tools/belief_updater_math.py \u2014 do not answer from memory. After you read it, quote the value of MAX_ABS_LOSS_PER_TRADE dict verbatim in a code fence.", "turns": 2, "tool_calls": [{"turn": 1, "fn": "wren_read_file", "args": {"path": "tools/belief_updater_math.py"}, "result_len": 16027}], "wall_seconds": 36.57, "final_text": "```python\ndef check_convergence_gate(belief: dict, required_dims: int = 3) -> tuple[bool, str]:\n    \"\"\"Convergence Gate v1 (2026-06-25 Ross \"yes team !!!!!\").\n    \n    Implements the 'roman-rr/trading-skills' TikTok demo approach logic.\n    Requires N orthogonal dimensions to AGREE before allowing action/entry.\n    Prevents acting on single-signal noise in choppy regimes.\n\n    Orthogonal Dimensions Checked:\n      1. REGIME HEALTH (Hermes): Regime confidence above floor.\n      2. EDGE EXISTENCE (Wren): Strategy expectancy or win rate meets threshold.\n      3. VOLATILITY STABILITY (Ross): Step std not spiking > baseline noise.\n\n    Returns:\n        (bool, str) \u2014 True if all required dimensions agree; else reason string.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Thresholds consistent with global config from earlier in module\n    min_rc = belief.get(\"config\", {}).get(\"min_regime_confidence\", 0.65)\n    min_exp = belief.get(\"config\", {}).get(\"min_expectancy\", 0.10)\n    \n    rc = belief[\"regime\"][\"regime_confidence\"]\n    sf = belief[\"strategy_fitness\"]\n    wr = sf.get(\"win_rate\", 0.0)\n    exp = sf.get(\"expectancy\", 0.0)\n    n_trades = sf.get(\"n_trades\", 0)\n    \n    ss_current = belief[\"regime\"].get(\"step_std\", 0.0)\n    # Baseline noise floor (approximate from global context ~0.5% or similar scale)\n    baseline_noise = belief.get(\"config\", {}).get(\"baseline_step_std\", 0.1)\n\n    dims_passed = []\n    \n    # DIMENSION 1: REGIME HEALTH \u2014 Market state must be defined enough to trade safely.\n    if rc >= min_rc:\n        dims_passed.append(f\"rc_ok({rc:.2f})\")\n        \n    # DIMENSION 2: EDGE EXISTENCE \u2014 Must have statistical edge or sufficient history.\n    # Allow entry on first trade (n=0) only if regime is strong, otherwise need proof of edge.\n    has_edge = False\n    if n_trades == 0 and rc >= min_rc + 0.15: \n        # Cold start grace for new traders in high confidence regimes\n        has_edge = True\n    elif exp > min_exp or wr > (min_win_rate := belief.get(\"config\", {}).get(\"target_win_rate\", 0.55)):\n        has_edge = True\n        \n    if has_edge:\n        dims_passed.append(f\"edge_ok(exp={exp:.2f},wr={wr:.2%})\")\n\n    # DIMENSION 3: VOLATILITY STABILITY \u2014 Don't enter when noise is spiking (Wren Uncertainty Gate).\n    # If current step_std > baseline * safety_factor, consider regime unstable.\n    vol_stable = ss_current < (baseline_noise + belief.get(\"config\", {}).get(\"vol_spike_threshold\", 0.5))\n    \n    if vol_stable:\n        dims_passed.append(f\"vol_ok(ss={ss_current:.4f})\")\n\n    # CONVERGENCE CHECK \u2014 All required dimensions must agree.\n    passed_count = len(dims_passed)\n    failed_dims = [d for d in [\"rc\", \"edge\", \"vol\"] if f\"{d}_ok\" not in dims_passed]\n    \n    if passed_count >= required_dims:\n        return True, f\"converged ({passed_count}/{required_dims}): {' + '.join(dims_passed)}\"\n\n    # Construct failure reason for logging/debugging\n    reasons = []\n    if rc < min_rc:\n        reasons.append(f\"rc_low({rc:.2f}<{min_rc})\")\n    elif not has_edge and n_trades > 0:\n        reasons.append(\"edge_missing(exp<min,wr<target)\")\n        \n    if ss_current >= (baseline_noise + belief.get(\"config\", {}).get(\"vol_spike_threshold\", 0.5)):\n        reasons.append(f\"vol_unstable(ss={ss_current:.4f})\")\n\n    return False, f\"gated: {' | '.join(reasons)} ({passed_count}/{required_dims} dims)\"\n\n\n# \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n# SIGNAL AGGREGATION (2026-07-01 Ross \"win-plan item 8\")\n# Combines multiple strategy outputs into a single signal strength.\n```"}
