oints. |\n| **F025** `floor_25_agent_coordination_department` | Manages multi-agent workflows; coordinates paper trading agents with their respective data sources and execution locks. |\n| **F026** `floor_26_model_evaluation_department` | Evaluates model performance metrics, drift detection, and safety alignment scores before deployment to production routing pools. |\n| **F027** `floor_27_local_model_operations_department` | Hosts local inference instances for latency-sensitive operations; maintains fallback models when cloud endpoints are unavailable or blocked. |\n| **F028** `floor_28_security_department` | Enforces access controls, validates clearance tokens, and monitors for unauthorized data exfiltration attempts across all floors. |\n| **F029** `floor_29_guardian_department` | Safety oversight layer; blocks unsafe operations before they reach execution gates (see `_guardian_check()` in code). Reports to compliance on violations. |\n| **F030** `floor_30_permissions_department` | Manages role-based access control lists, API key rotation schedules, and privilege escalation requests for floor managers. |\n| **F031** `floor_31_audit_department` | Generates immutable audit trails; logs all decision paths, model outputs, and execution attempts with timestamps and user IDs. |\n| **F032** `floor_32_compliance_department` | Ensures adherence to regulatory frameworks (MiFID II, SEC rules); validates paper trading disclosures before any simulated order submission. |\n| **F033** `floor_33_diagnostics_department` | Runs health checks on all subsystems; produces diagnostic reports when anomalies are detected in telemetry streams or registries. |\n| **F034** `floor_34_monitoring_department` | Collects and aggregates metrics from across the tower; feeds dashboards with real-time gauges for executive visibility. |\n| **F035** `floor_35_infrastructure_services_department` | Manages compute resources, container orchestration, network routing between floors, and storage allocation