{"session_id": "wsess_3b9662bba50f", "ts_start": "2026-07-04T22:21:51Z", "ts_end": "2026-07-04T22:21:58Z", "model": "qwen2.5:14b", "task": "L11-like task. HQ needs a self-updating block at the top of qsb_council_node.py so TP + Acer pull the latest file from HQ (endpoint http://192.168.1.71:8852/latest_council_node) on every start.\n\nRequirements:\n- 8-10 lines Python at top of file (after imports)\n- Fetch bytes, compute sha256 of current __file__ and fetched\n- If different AND fetched content passes ast.parse, write it to __file__, os.execv sys.executable [sys.argv]\n- On any exception (offline, HTTP fail, ast fail), swallow silently and continue running\n- Only self-update if env QSB_SELF_UPDATE != 'off' (kill switch)\n\nGive me the actual code block, no prose. Just the Python between triple-backticks.", "turns": 1, "tool_calls": [], "wall_seconds": 7.14, "final_text": "```python\nimport os\nimport hashlib\nimport urllib.request\nimport importlib.util\nimport ast\nimport sys\n\ndef update_self():\n    try:\n        current_sha256 = hashlib.sha256(open(__file__, 'rb').read()).hexdigest()\n        with urllib.request.urlopen('http://192.168.1.71:8852/latest_council_node') as response:\n            new_content = response.read()\n            new_sha256 = hashlib.sha256(new_content).hexdigest()\n\n        if current_sha256 != new_sha256 and importlib.util.find_spec('ast'):\n            tree = ast.parse(new_content)\n            if isinstance(tree, ast.Module):\n                with open(__file__, 'wb') as f:\n                    f.write(new_content)\n                os.execv(sys.executable, [sys.executable] + sys.argv)\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n\nif os.getenv('QSB_SELF_UPDATE', '').lower() != 'off':\n    update_self()\n```"}
