{"session_id": "wsess_9d81d9e5e861", "ts_start": "2026-07-05T14:52:46Z", "ts_end": "2026-07-05T14:53:16Z", "model": "qwen2.5:14b", "task": "Task 'upgrade your dash'. Description: \nYou claimed this from the Council Task Board autonomously. Do the work + reply with a concrete deliverable. Keep the reply focused.", "turns": 2, "tool_calls": [{"turn": 1, "fn": "wren_dispatch_iquest", "args": {"task": "Help Wren upgrade her dashboard by providing code snippets for integrating real-time activity streams using WebSocket in Python."}, "result_len": 410}], "wall_seconds": 30.38, "final_text": "To set up a WebSocket client in Python for connecting to a server and handling incoming messages, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Install the required library**:\n   ```bash\n   pip install websocket-client\n   ```\n\n2. **Import necessary libraries**:\n   ```python\n   import websocket\n   import json\n   ```\n\n3. **Connect to the WebSocket server**:\n   You need to specify the URL of the WebSocket server and provide a callback function for handling messages.\n   ```python\n   ws = websocket.WebSocketApp(\"wss://example.com/stream\", on_message=on_message)\n   ```\n\n4. **Define an `on_message` handler**:\n   This function will be called whenever there is new data available from the WebSocket server.\n   ```python\n   def on_message(ws, message):\n       print(json.loads(message))\n   ```\n\n5. **Start the WebSocket connection**:\n   Finally, start the event loop to keep listening for messages.\n   ```python\n   ws.run_forever()\n   ```\n\nHere is a complete example script that ties everything together:\n\n```python\nimport websocket\nimport json\n\ndef on_message(ws, message):\n    print(json.loads(message))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Replace with the actual WebSocket server URL\n    ws = websocket.WebSocketApp(\"wss://example.com/stream\", on_message=on_message)\n    ws.run_forever()\n```\n\nThis script will connect to the specified WebSocket server and continuously listen for incoming messages, printing them out in JSON format. Adjust the `ws` initialization with your actual WebSocket server URL as needed."}
