: scale(1); }\n  50% { transform: scale(1.2); }\n}\n\n.task-state-flash {\n  animation-name: task-state-bounce;\n  animation-duration: 500ms;\n}\n```\n\n### JavaScript (`task_state_animation.js`)\n\n```javascript\nfunction updateTaskState(taskId, newState) {\n  const taskElement = document.getElementById(`task-${taskId}`);\n  if (taskElement) {\n    taskElement.classList.add('task-state-flash');\n    setTimeout(() => taskElement.classList.remove('task-state-flash'), 500);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThese files will handle the bounce/flash animation when a task changes state. The JavaScript function `updateTaskState` can be called whenever a task transitions to a new state, triggering the CSS animation.\n\nThis completes the task of creating micro-animations for state transitions in tasks. If you need any further adjustments or additional features, let me know!"}
